31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My research shows that regional scanning contractors have unreliable delivery windows that shift based on other clients. However, the community halls north of the river remained operational despite the winter road closures.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh wow, I found something really important! The outer wards lost their bus links, so people there have a super long trip now. But the old outreach stops were actually more popular than the main building!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,George,,"It appears our funding structure is problematic. The county grants only cover the first year of session fees, and we are seeing a pattern where operational costs, like vehicle running, are overshooting their budgets.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,May,,"It's funny how we always imagine the new stuff is the hard part. I found that some evening groups from six years ago are still thriving on their own, while a digitisation project from the same era just flopped.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that we have some skilled retired tradespeople volunteering, but... it seems no one on the staff is actually trained to supervise them. Also, the person who certified our power tools retired in spring.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if vehicle running costs are overshooting, we must be cautious about any expansion that relies on mobile services or frequent transport.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that's a good point, but we can't just ignore the outer wards! They really need us since the buses stopped running, and they used to love the outreach stops.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I understand the need, but we must be realistic. If the funding for session fees vanishes after a year and vehicle costs are already too high, a mobile service could become a financial burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're so focused on the budget! But look at the data—people are using the catalogue late at night. Why are we worrying about cars when the digital demand is peaking while we're locked up?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with George that we should be careful. If we start something new, we have to make sure we actually have the people to manage it... not just the money.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, digital demand is high, but we must consider the infrastructure. If we rely on external contractors for digitisation, my findings suggest the delivery windows are unstable and subject to the whims of larger clients.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@May, I love the idea of digital access, but if people in the outer wards can't even get to a branch, maybe we need something that brings the library to them? It's so sad they're cut off!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, it is indeed unfortunate, but a mobile solution is a liability if the grant only covers the first year. We cannot start a service that we are forced to cut in twelve months.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,May,,"@Yumi, bringing the library to them is a lovely sentiment, but why reinvent the wheel? Some of our old community groups are still going strong without us. Maybe the answer isn't a fancy new bus, but something more sustainable.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just worry that if we add more to the staff's plate, they'll be overwhelmed. Especially if we need specific certifications or supervision skills that we don't actually have on the roster right now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your point about supervision is critical. If we lack the internal capacity to manage a project, it becomes another point of failure. We need a solution that is stable, self-sufficient, and independent of external contractors.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I totally agree that we need stability! But maybe we can find a way to help the outer wards that doesn't rely on expensive buses or fancy contractors? I just can't stand the thought of them being left behind!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,George,,We must avoid the trap of short-term enthusiasm. A project that looks successful in its first year but drains our operating budget in the second is not a service; it is a liability.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,May,,"You're all being so dramatic! Let's just be honest: we're terrified of failing. But we've already failed before—like that digitisation mess—and we've succeeded without trying. We need something that lasts, not a flash in the pan.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I just want us to be kind to the staff. If we pick something that requires a lot of specialized oversight, and we don't have it, it will just be... stressful for everyone.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
