56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I lean toward Candidate A. It relies on community partners and facilitators rather than external contractors or expensive vehicles, making it the most stable and least vulnerable to the disruptions I've identified.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I really want to support Candidate D because it helps the people in the outer wards who lost their buses! But George is right about the money, and I don't want it to fail. Maybe A is a good compromise?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,George,,"I cannot support Candidate D; the vehicle costs and short-term grant structure make it a financial risk. Candidate B relies on contractors, and C requires certifications we lack. Candidate A is the most sustainable choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,May,,"A is definitely the safest bet, but let's be real: B is just a repeat of that digitisation disaster from six years ago. Why would we try that again? A is sustainable and actually works.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate A is the best. Candidate C would be too hard because we don't have anyone to certify the tools anymore, and I don't want the staff to be stressed. A seems... safer.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, Candidate A allows us to reach those outer wards through partner organizations and community halls, which I found remain operational even when roads are difficult. It provides the access you want without the risks George and I fear.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that's such a wonderful way to look at it! If we can use community halls, we can still reach the people who are cut off without needing a big, expensive bus. I'm feeling much better about A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, your point about the community halls is a sound one. By leveraging existing local infrastructure, we avoid the operational overruns associated with vehicles and the instability of short-term grants. Candidate A is the only rational choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, for once, we agree! It's a relief to see you're not just counting pennies. A is the only one that doesn't feel like a gamble or a ghost of a failed project. I'm in.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm glad everyone is agreeing. Candidate A doesn't seem to require the specialized technical supervision that Candidate C would, so it won't put too much pressure on the staff. I feel comfortable with A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"It is clear that Candidate A is the most resilient option. It avoids the contractor delays of B, the certification gaps of C, and the financial and logistical instability of D. It is the most logical path.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so happy we found a way to help everyone! Candidate A is just perfect because it's kind to the staff, safe for the budget, and still reaches the people who need us most. I vote for A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,George,,I concur. Candidate A aligns with our financial realities and avoids the pitfalls of the other proposals. It is a sustainable investment that will not collapse once the initial grant expires. I vote for A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,May,,I'll stop playing the devil's advocate since you've all finally come to your senses. A is the only choice that isn't a total disaster waiting to happen. I vote for A!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree with everyone. Candidate A is the most thoughtful choice for the staff and the community. I vote for A.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. Candidate A is the only proposal that ensures continuity by relying on stable, local conditions rather than volatile external factors. I vote for A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so glad we're all on the same page! Let's make this happen for the community!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
